#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643302 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b043f4d-a341-5b61-855b-76770e803196" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643314} {:answer/id #uuid "af9e7843-2bac-5513-b4d2-7dd7e1a0fa52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643318} {:answer/id #uuid "cc9ba515-fc97-5551-97ec-93537721f718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643323} {:answer/id #uuid "e129dd58-a0db-5850-bc30-232d21c53170" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643324} {:answer/id #uuid "f62e89d2-63ef-5980-8e1d-895b89e30ebd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643326}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643314} :answer-field/id #uuid "38b3db48-afa1-58f0-a70f-9bbf2c4a9dab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643305}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2d5b8136-3aa3-595e-a435-3170a438f38d" :question/problem "![](images/0b/0bbf58f80060415a5f773150d354f0548fbb37f9617929e4f86929e78ef1c572.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=5$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643312 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3da5abfd-b2f1-56a5-91e8-9ec150222b01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643307}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643307} :answer-field/id #uuid "b339082a-5e0a-5e99-9892-39a183fff595" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "81a18912-3a04-554c-8ece-d62e8b2acca3" :question/problem "![](images/4e/4eb7e5fed25a147865a356a491c551d745f58730ad9c3fe4c333c6f2e0d1cfca.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=9$ and the vertical radius has length $b=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{9}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643313 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22519a3e-bc57-5bda-a294-ac35c6688b50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643300} {:answer/id #uuid "50a9aa28-fa7c-511d-8f1c-55d32b0d4759" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643308} {:answer/id #uuid "